{
 "<i>Body Wisdom</i>": "",
 "-Breathwork Ceremony-": "",
 "JULY 25, 2026 LISBON, PORTUGAL": "",
 "Dhara by Sadhana": "",
 "Lisbon, Portugal": "",
 "July 25th": "",
 "Saturday": "",
 "9.00am - 13.30pm": "",
 "1/2 day experience": "",
 "Your body has been keeping score long before<br>your mind caught up.": "",
 "<em>It knows fear</em> before you can name it.<br><em>It knows safety</em> before you understand it.<br><em>It knows love, loss, effort and exhaustion</em> long before the mind has the language to explain it.": "",
 "<i>This ceremony is an invitation to come back.</i>": "",
 "<a> <span> <span>Book my Spot</span> </span> </a>": "",
 "What If your body had the answer?": "",
 "Before you had words for things, your body already knew.": "",
 "<span>If you have ever felt a tightness in your chest that has no clear reason or noticed your shoulders are up around your ears before you even realise you are tense. <br>If you have ever felt a wave of something move through you and have no idea where it came from.</span>": "",
 "<span><b>That is the body speaking</b></span>": "",
 "Every injury you push through.<br>Every moment you hold your breath in a difficult conversation.<br>Every time you carry something alone and keep moving anyway.": "",
 "The body is there for all of it. Taking notes and storing what never gets processed… waiting for the moment you slow down enough to listen.": "",
 "This ceremony creates the conditions for the body to do what it already knows how to do: to release what it has been carrying and to remember what it has always known. Your body is the oldest and wisest part of you and this afternoon is simply a chance to finally let it speak.": "",
 "the flow": "",
 "What this experience <i>holds</i>": "",
 "<span>All practices honour personal boundaries and the pace of each individual. <br>I will create a trusting and supportive environment where you can explore your authenticity in complete safety and freedom.</span>": "",
 "Movement &amp; Somatic Awakening": "",
 "We begin in the body. Gentle somatic practices and guided movement to drop out of the thinking mind and into felt experience.": "",
 "Connection &amp; Presence": "",
 "Simple partner and group practices that build a felt sense of safety, trust and genuine contact. The kind of connection that goes beyond words.": "",
 "A 50-60 minute guided breathwork journey using continuous rhythmic breathing, music and sound. This practice has a way of bypassing the thinking mind entirely and taking you somewhere the mind alone cannot go.": "",
 "What is <i>Breathwork</i>?": "",
 "<strong>Conscious Connected Breathwork</strong> is a rhythmic breathing practice done lying down, with music, in a safe and held space. The breath stays continuous, without pauses, which gradually shifts the state of the nervous system and opens access to parts of yourself that are harder to reach in ordinary awareness.": "",
 "The breath has a way of taking you somewhere the mind alone cannot go. <em>Inner landscapes you didn’t know existed.</em> <br>A quieter, older part of yourself that has been waiting for space. Sometimes what arises is deep relaxation. Sometimes it is clarity. <br>Sometimes the nervous system completes a cycle it never had the chance to finish. Sometimes an emotion moves through you that you couldn’t have predicted and wouldn’t know how to explain.": "",
 "<strong>The approach here is not cathartic.</strong> The body is treated like an onion, worked with in layers, at its own pace. Each person receives what they need in that moment and no specific outcome is ever the goal. This removes any pressure to feel or do anything in particular, and creates the conditions for something genuine to emerge.": "",
 "In Their Own Words": "",
 "I‘d say it was breath-taking but it was quite the opposite: breath-giving, amazing, beautiful. Fabio has a way of holding the space &amp; guiding carefully that helped me to encounter myself deeply. It was the most beautiful breathwork-experience so far for me. Big recommendations &amp; thanks again": "",
 "<strong>Katerina</strong> <span></span>": "",
 "Fabio is truly a master guide on the breathwork journey. Breathwork with Fabio has been a constant instrument in changing my life for the better ever since I took the first session. From external environment to internal shifts, I am grateful to have experienced a change in both.": "",
 "<strong>Tamás Józsa</strong> <span></span>": "",
 "My first breathwork session with Fabio was unforgettable. By the end, I felt like a baby - soft, calm, and completely safe. The way he guides the breath has rhythm and flow, lifting you up and grounding you down until you reach that sweet, magical spot - your very first breath": "",
 "I’ve been recommending him to all my friends, because it’s rare to meet someone who works with so much care and presence.": "",
 "<strong>Simona Andreea Badoiu</strong> <span></span>": "",
 "About me": "",
 "Fabio cancogni": "",
 "I didn’t find breathwork through curiosity. I found it through necessity: a<span>fter going through a difficult period with my mental health, the breath became the first thing that actually worked as a direct way back to myself. <br>That experience changed the direction of everything.</span>": "",
 "What followed was years of working close to the edges of human experience. <br>I trained in<i> trauma-informed approaches</i> and worked with medical patients navigating stress, anxiety and nervous system dysregulation. <br>I brought breathwork into sport, working with high-performance athletes and was part of the support team at the Paris Olympics. Each context taught me something different about what the body holds and what it needs to let go.": "",
 "Today I work primarily with CEOs, founders and leaders who are high-functioning on the outside and quietly running on empty on the inside. People who have built a lot and somewhere along the way lost the thread back to themselves. The breath, in my experience, is the fastest and most honest way back.": "",
 "My approach is science-grounded, trauma-aware and deeply intuitive. I listen to what is alive in the room and work with it. Every session is shaped around what the person or group actually needs in that moment.": "",
 "The Venue": "",
 "dhara by sadhana | lisbon": "",
 "<strong>Dhara by Sadhana</strong> is one of those rare spaces in Lisbon that feels different the moment you walk in. Tucked away in a quiet street, it carries a quality of stillness that most spaces in the city simply don’t have. Warm, sacred, alive with the energy of everything that has been held within its walls.": "",
 "It was chosen deliberately for this ceremony. A space that already knows how to hold people. Where the walls carry a sense of something quieter than the city outside. Where the light falls in a way that makes slowing down feel natural.": "",
 "This is your <i>Invitation</i>": "",
 "If something in you is already saying yes, trust that.": "",
 "July 25th | 9.00am - 13.30pm | Dhara by Sadhana": "",
 "Investment: 66€": "",
 "<a> <span> <span>Book your Spot NOW!</span> </span> </a>": "",
 "Safety &amp; Considerations": "",
 "Breathwork is generally safe when practiced with proper guidance": "",
 "However, certain conditions require caution or medical clearance. Safety is always the priority.": "",
 "Please consult with me before attending if you have:": "",
 "Do I need any prior experience?": "",
 "No. Whether this is your first time in a breathwork or somatic space, or you have done this many times before, you will be met where you are. There is no right or wrong way to show up": "",
 "What will I actually feel during the practice?": "",
 "<br>It varies from person to person. Some people feel warmth or tingling moving through the body. Some feel heaviness, then a release into lightness. Some feel emotion rise and pass. Some feel a deep stillness they haven't touched in a long time. The honest answer is that you won't know until you are in it, and that is part of what makes it worth doing.": "",
 "What if something intense comes up?": "",
 "The practice is designed in layers. Nothing is forced and the body is always respected. If at any point it feels like too much, you can simply return to normal breathing and the intensity settles quickly. I am present throughout and will notice if you need support before you even have to ask.": "",
 "Will I be okay to go about my day afterwards?": "",
 "Most people leave feeling grounded, clear, and quietly open. Some feel a little tender, in a good way, like something has shifted and needs a moment to settle. It is worth keeping the afternoon gentle if you can. A big social event straight after is not ideal, but most people drive home without any issue.": "",
 "Who usually comes to these sessions?": "",
 "<br>People at different points in their lives. Some going through a transition, some simply curious, some who have tried everything else and want to try something that works from the inside out. What they tend to have in common is a sense that there is more available to them than what they are currently accessing. You will not be the only first-timer in the room.": "",
 "Why a group and not a private session?": "",
 "There is something that happens in a group that cannot be replicated alone. When one person gives themselves permission to go deeper, it creates a kind of permission for everyone else. The shared energy of the room becomes part of the experience. Many people find their first group session more powerful than they expected precisely because of this.": "",
 "Ready to listen to your body?": "",
 "Spots are limited to keep the group intimate. Once they are gone, they are gone.": "",
