 "js:A pause": "",
 "js:Your nervous system does not really tell the difference between a genuine threat and a full inbox. Both can trigger the same response: a faster heart rate, a shorter breath, a body that stays ready to act.": "",
 "js:When that response gets used often enough, it stops feeling like stress and starts feeling like personality. That reaction is a pattern your body learned early, built to keep you safe. It just never learned when to switch off.": "",
